.TH SWAP 3
.SH NAME
swap \- integral representation conversion routines
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f(CW#include <swap.h>\fP
.sp
\f(CWssize_t swapop(const void* internal, const void* external, ssize_t width);\fP
.br
\f(CWintmax_t swapget(int op, const void* from, size_t width);\fP
.br
\f(CWvoid* swapput(int op, void* to, size_t width, intmax_t value);\fP
.br
\f(CWvoid* swapmem(int op, const void* from, void* to, size_t n);\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
These routines convert integral constants between internal and
external representations.
They are used to handle binary data generated by foreign programs.
New binary data representations should use the compact canonical form
provided by the
.IR sfio (3)
routines
\f(CWsfputu\fP
and
\f(CWsgetu\fR.
.PP
\f(CWswapop\fP
returns the swap operation required to convert the
\f(CWwidth\fP
byte integer
\f(CWexternal\fP
to the
\f(CWwidth\fP
byte integer
\f(CWinternal\fR.
The swap operation is a bit mask:
.TP
\f(CW0\fP
No swapping necessary.
.TP
\f(CW1\fP
Swap byte
\f(CW0\fP
with byte
\f(CW1\fR.
.TP
\f(CW2\fP
Swap bytes
\f(CW0\fP
and
\f(CW1\fP
with bytes
\f(CW2\fP
and
\f(CW3\fR.
.TP
\f(CW4\fP
Swap bytes
\f(CW0-3\fP
with bytes
\f(CW4-7\fR,
and so on.
The largest native integral type is defined by the type
\f(CWintmax_t\fP
from the header
\f(CW<ast.h>\fR.
.PP
\f(CWswapget\fP
returns the
\f(CWwidth\fP
byte integer in the buffer
\f(CWfrom\fR,
swapped according to
\f(CWop\fR.
.PP
\f(CWswapput\fP
copies the
\f(CWwidth\fP
byte integer
\f(CWvalue\fP
into the buffer
\f(CWto\fR,
swapped according to
\f(CWop\fR.
\f(CWto\fP
is returned.
.PP
\f(CWswapmem\fP
swaps
\f(CWn\fP
bytes from the buffer
\f(CWfrom\fP
to the buffer
\f(CWto\fP
according to
\f(CWop\fR.
\f(CWto\fP
and
\f(CWfrom\fP
may be the same.
